WEBVTT

00:13.600 --> 00:17.080
♪ Take a walk
To the edge of town ♪

00:17.200 --> 00:19.920
♪ And go across the tracks ♪

00:22.320 --> 00:24.840
♪ Where the viaduct looms ♪

00:24.960 --> 00:27.200
♪ Like a bird of doom ♪

00:27.320 --> 00:31.320
♪ As it shifts and cracks ♪

00:32.439 --> 00:37.320
♪ Where secrets lie
In the border fires ♪

00:37.440 --> 00:40.120
♪ In the humming wires ♪

00:40.200 --> 00:41.360
♪ Hey man ♪

00:41.440 --> 00:43.920
♪ You're never coming back ♪

00:44.000 --> 00:46.320
♪ Past the square
Past the bridge ♪

00:46.440 --> 00:49.520
♪ Past the mills
Past the stacks ♪

00:52.640 --> 00:55.280
♪ On a gathering storm comes ♪

00:55.360 --> 00:57.720
♪ A tall handsome man ♪

00:57.800 --> 01:00.520
♪ In a dusty black coat with ♪

01:00.600 --> 01:03.800
♪ A red right hand ♪

01:07.200 --> 01:09.840
♪ Red right hand ♪

01:11.880 --> 01:15.080
♪ The red right hand ♪

01:18.800 --> 01:22.440
[crowd cheering in distance]

01:40.120 --> 01:41.680
Yeah, you're like me, Tommy,

01:41.760 --> 01:44.720
you can't bear to watch a fight
which has got rules.

01:48.360 --> 01:49.920
Tommy, right, imagine...

01:51.160 --> 01:53.520
Imagine that you could not see...

01:55.240 --> 01:58.320
at all, you was born blind.

01:59.440 --> 02:03.320
Then one day you open up your eyes

02:04.240 --> 02:07.840
and you can see everything

02:08.440 --> 02:09.720
in the world.

02:10.880 --> 02:12.840
When before you could only

02:13.600 --> 02:15.320
touch it or smell it.

02:17.000 --> 02:17.880
There it is.

02:19.640 --> 02:20.680
The revelation.

02:21.880 --> 02:22.800
Innit?

02:26.800 --> 02:27.880
I've had one.

02:29.920 --> 02:32.520
Yeah, saw a beautiful house
down in Margate.

02:32.600 --> 02:34.600
Great big white building...

02:35.600 --> 02:38.560
Monkey puzzle tree against a sky of blue.

02:39.920 --> 02:41.880
Beautiful. A piece of heaven.

02:41.960 --> 02:46.800
Actually, you see, the way the Earth,
it curves, I thought to myself,

02:46.880 --> 02:49.960
"Alfie, what are you doing?

02:52.040 --> 02:53.480
What are you doing?

02:53.840 --> 02:56.960
Why don't you just sell
every ounce of gold and sell

02:57.040 --> 03:00.840
every barrel of rum you got and just
buy yourself some time, mate?"

03:04.120 --> 03:06.520
I need to buy myself some time.

03:08.280 --> 03:09.360
You're moving to Margate?

03:09.600 --> 03:12.880
I am actually, yeah.
I need to get myself some rest.

03:12.960 --> 03:14.440
I need some rest.

03:15.480 --> 03:17.600
Plus, the Americans are here now,
aren't they?

03:17.680 --> 03:19.320
So, that's it.

03:19.400 --> 03:23.040
Yeah. It's been that way ever since
the war, innit? The Americans.

03:24.800 --> 03:28.920
Big fucks small.

03:30.280 --> 03:31.960
Always, actually.

03:32.560 --> 03:33.480
Hmm?

03:34.000 --> 03:39.760
And there is a fight going on,
out there, between big and small.

03:42.040 --> 03:45.520
Big will fuck small.

03:50.120 --> 03:54.520
Right. Margate then. Blue skies, heaven.

03:58.920 --> 04:00.840
I will see you, Tommy.

04:02.880 --> 04:04.000
By the pier.

04:06.840 --> 04:08.360
Stay and watch the fight, Alfie?

04:10.000 --> 04:11.000
No, you're all right.

04:12.680 --> 04:14.560
I already know who wins.

04:15.320 --> 04:16.200
Don't I?

04:24.520 --> 04:25.400
Cheer up.

04:32.680 --> 04:34.480
[man shouting]

04:38.760 --> 04:40.600
[bell rings]

04:40.680 --> 04:42.160
[referee] Round one!

04:42.240 --> 04:44.360
[crowd clamoring]

04:47.520 --> 04:49.600
-Left, right.
-[sniffing]

04:56.680 --> 04:58.920
[indistinct shouting]

05:05.520 --> 05:07.280
[grunting]

05:07.360 --> 05:10.160
[yelling]

05:11.080 --> 05:12.840
-[grunts]
-[crowd cheering]

05:19.440 --> 05:20.520
-[crowd] Oh!
-[bell ringing]

05:22.960 --> 05:24.160
Bonnie! Bonnie!

05:25.120 --> 05:26.120
[Speaking Romani]
You're ok son?

05:28.240 --> 05:29.800
It's under control?

05:30.560 --> 05:32.000
I'll take it to the fourth.

05:33.920 --> 05:35.640
[in English] I know he's a big bastard
but you got to...

05:35.720 --> 05:38.320
-Where's Solomons?
-Apparently he doesn't watch.

05:39.000 --> 05:40.240
[Arthur] Look at that corner. Look.

05:40.600 --> 05:42.640
The men there, they don't know fighters.

05:42.720 --> 05:44.120
I don't like it.

05:44.560 --> 05:46.400
You feel it though, Tom, don't ya?

05:46.480 --> 05:48.400
I feel it. We're all right.

05:48.520 --> 05:50.480
We're surrounded by soldiers, Arthur.

05:50.640 --> 05:53.320
Alfie's men were strip searched.
We're all right.

05:54.840 --> 05:56.720
Right, come on, Gypsy boy, let's go.

05:56.800 --> 05:58.120
-[cheering]
-Round two!

05:59.400 --> 06:01.360
[indistinct shouting]

06:06.040 --> 06:07.720
[grunting]

06:10.600 --> 06:11.960
[door opens]

06:20.800 --> 06:22.800
[Polly] So what did Tommy say
when you told him?

06:24.240 --> 06:26.280
He said I'd get a weekly allowance.

06:26.400 --> 06:27.960
[Polly] Oh, he can be romantic.

06:28.040 --> 06:29.480
[door opens]

06:30.560 --> 06:32.280
Of course as company treasurer,

06:32.360 --> 06:34.440
I shall be questioning that expense.

06:34.520 --> 06:37.640
He said something like, "We've had
enough death, let's have some life."

06:37.720 --> 06:39.480
-[door opens]
-Poll...

06:40.560 --> 06:42.400
This fight is fixed, isn't it?

06:43.160 --> 06:45.120
Poor Gypsy boy's getting
battered out there.

06:45.760 --> 06:47.720
Right. You said you have some news?

06:48.000 --> 06:49.360
Lizzie has some news.

06:49.800 --> 06:50.720
Polly.

06:50.960 --> 06:52.600
Well, tell her. Now!

06:52.680 --> 06:54.360
While the men are screaming for blood.

06:55.040 --> 06:57.160
Have a swig. You're gonna need it.

06:59.080 --> 07:00.160
I'm up the duff.

07:02.320 --> 07:03.480
And it's Tommy's.

07:05.320 --> 07:06.440
How far gone are you?

07:06.520 --> 07:08.520
If I were going to London
I'd be in Coventry.

07:08.920 --> 07:10.600
And are you carrying on past Coventry?

07:10.680 --> 07:12.400
All the way to fucking Piccadilly Circus.

07:12.480 --> 07:14.440
You found out whether
she's having a boy or a girl, Poll?

07:14.720 --> 07:15.560
No.

07:15.640 --> 07:16.480
Go on then.

07:23.840 --> 07:25.600
[giggling]

07:26.680 --> 07:27.680
It's a girl.

07:29.680 --> 07:30.640
Call her Ruby.

07:31.280 --> 07:32.400
Ruby Shelby.

07:33.200 --> 07:35.520
She'll be a star in a Hollywood movie.

07:37.040 --> 07:37.960
Hmm.

07:39.120 --> 07:40.360
Congratulations.

07:40.440 --> 07:42.560
[door opens]

07:42.640 --> 07:44.760
-[crowd cheering in distance]
-Hey, Linda.

07:44.840 --> 07:48.480
Welcome to the extraordinary general
meeting of the Shelby ladies club.

07:48.560 --> 07:50.560
[all laughing]

07:50.640 --> 07:51.960
Is there spit on my back?

07:52.640 --> 07:55.560
There were men out there spitting.
It's fucking disgusting.

07:55.640 --> 07:57.800
No, there's no spit on your back.

07:59.520 --> 08:02.120
Don't let us stop you doing
what you came in to do.

08:03.800 --> 08:04.640
What?

08:06.080 --> 08:09.360
It's helped me get through the fucking
nightmare of being stuck in this city.

08:11.000 --> 08:14.160
Well, since you're here
and you're almost family,

08:14.640 --> 08:15.960
Lizzie's got some news.

08:16.360 --> 08:18.480
-I'm pregnant.
-[Linda] Oh?

08:19.800 --> 08:22.480
And who's the father, have you
managed to narrow it down?

08:24.160 --> 08:25.600
[snorting]

08:27.160 --> 08:28.880
Yes, it's Tommy.

08:29.520 --> 08:30.800
Congratulations.

08:31.400 --> 08:33.080
You've won the raffle at last.

08:33.840 --> 08:36.440
Yeah. She's a real Shelby lady now, Linda.

08:37.480 --> 08:38.640
Just like you.

08:39.360 --> 08:42.320
Right, ladies, let's rejoin our gentlemen.

08:42.880 --> 08:44.280
And just remember, Linda,

08:44.680 --> 08:47.320
if they spit, just spit back.

08:48.240 --> 08:49.760
[chuckling]

08:50.680 --> 08:52.840
-I'll see you out there.
-[Polly] All right.

08:53.880 --> 08:55.880
[crowd clamoring]

08:57.360 --> 08:58.480
Come on, Bonnie!

09:01.280 --> 09:03.360
[crowd cheering]

09:04.440 --> 09:05.600
Put him away!

09:12.120 --> 09:14.640
Right. Who's with me, boys?

09:16.800 --> 09:19.440
Come get your loyalty, boy.

09:19.880 --> 09:21.240
You still in control, Bonnie?

09:22.080 --> 09:23.080
Yes.

09:23.840 --> 09:24.840
Then take him.

09:26.560 --> 09:27.960
[indistinct shouting]

09:28.240 --> 09:29.880
I give ya two to one!

09:30.200 --> 09:33.400
On the big Cockney Goliath, here.

09:33.640 --> 09:35.160
Take it or leave it, boys.

09:35.480 --> 09:37.320
Take it or leave it, boys.

09:37.560 --> 09:39.840
Two to one! Two to one!

09:40.800 --> 09:42.560
Look at them men in his corner. Look.

09:44.440 --> 09:45.920
They don't know fighters.

09:46.040 --> 09:48.000
They don't know the fucking ropes.

09:48.080 --> 09:50.520
It's the pills and the booze
spooking you, Arthur.

09:51.680 --> 09:52.960
-Round three!
-[cheering]

09:59.040 --> 10:00.160
[inaudible]

10:00.240 --> 10:03.360
Ah, look at them. They don't
stand right. They don't move right.

10:03.840 --> 10:06.200
They don't even care if he fucking wins.

10:08.240 --> 10:10.600
It's the fucking pills, brother.
All right?

10:21.160 --> 10:24.360
-Come on, Bonnie!
-[women cheering]

10:28.400 --> 10:29.800
[all shouting]

10:35.480 --> 10:37.840
Whoo! Come on, Bonnie!

10:38.120 --> 10:39.600
What the fuck are they laughing at?

10:40.920 --> 10:42.120
[Arthur] It's that new batch.

10:42.600 --> 10:43.600
Too strong.

10:45.720 --> 10:49.400
-[Polly] Come on, Bonnie!
-[all cheering]

10:49.480 --> 10:50.480
[sniffs]

10:51.080 --> 10:52.640
[crowd shouting]

10:56.680 --> 10:58.680
[Tommy] Arthur, leave it.
Where is he going?

10:58.760 --> 11:01.080
Sit down and watch the fight, eh, Arthur!

11:01.240 --> 11:02.240
Come here!

11:02.560 --> 11:04.840
Let me do my fucking job!

11:05.400 --> 11:07.720
[indistinct shouting]

11:11.400 --> 11:12.800
[sniffs]

11:13.720 --> 11:15.080
[grunts]

11:52.520 --> 11:54.000
[crowd cheering]

11:57.200 --> 11:58.080
Bonnie!

11:58.320 --> 12:00.160
Bonnie! Are you okay?

12:05.920 --> 12:09.200
I'll give you two to one
now on the Cockney.

12:09.280 --> 12:11.760
[crowd clamoring]

12:15.720 --> 12:16.760
[Arthur] Right.

12:18.880 --> 12:20.560
[exhales]

12:35.400 --> 12:37.320
[man] That's it. One, two. One, two!

12:42.800 --> 12:44.600
[crowd cheering]

12:45.320 --> 12:47.160
Come on, Bonnie boy!

12:47.240 --> 12:49.040
Bonnie, come on, kill him!

13:02.840 --> 13:04.840
[indistinct shouting]

13:09.240 --> 13:10.200
Come on!

13:10.760 --> 13:12.360
Where are Tommy and Arthur?

13:12.880 --> 13:14.200
[man] Punch him!

13:14.280 --> 13:15.200
I don't know.

13:17.160 --> 13:18.320
Come on, Bonnie!

13:19.080 --> 13:20.360
Come on!

13:26.040 --> 13:27.480
[clears throat]

13:28.800 --> 13:30.800
[breathing heavily]

13:46.720 --> 13:47.720
Arthur!

13:59.760 --> 14:01.200
[choking]

14:17.120 --> 14:19.360
[groaning] You fucking bastard.

14:21.600 --> 14:23.480
[choking]

14:37.080 --> 14:39.640
[panting]

14:42.120 --> 14:43.320
[gun clicks]

14:43.720 --> 14:44.920
[gunshot]

14:48.000 --> 14:48.920
Arthur!

15:56.400 --> 15:58.160
[inaudible]

16:07.840 --> 16:09.280
[yells]

16:22.560 --> 16:24.360
[inaudible]

16:24.440 --> 16:27.880
[referee] I declare Bonnie Gold the new
welterweight champion...

16:27.960 --> 16:29.680
of the Midlands South...

16:31.320 --> 16:32.320
Yes!

16:32.800 --> 16:35.240
Yes! Bonnie!

16:35.440 --> 16:36.520
Tommy, what's happened?

16:37.920 --> 16:39.000
Arthur's dead.

16:39.640 --> 16:41.400
[panting] He's dead.

16:43.680 --> 16:45.360
[inaudible]

16:46.920 --> 16:48.720
[crowd cheering]

16:54.920 --> 16:56.600
Tommy, we have the other wop.

16:57.200 --> 16:58.760
Cunt had a wire in his pocket.

17:00.560 --> 17:01.960
[grunting]

17:08.280 --> 17:09.280
Go on, Finn!

17:11.040 --> 17:12.040
Go on, Finn!

17:12.240 --> 17:13.560
[groaning]

17:15.440 --> 17:16.560
Take his eyes, Finn.

17:17.560 --> 17:18.680
Do it for Arthur.

17:21.000 --> 17:22.599
Take his fucking eyes!

17:26.599 --> 17:28.079
No. No!

17:31.560 --> 17:33.200
[man screaming]

17:48.400 --> 17:49.760
Close the doors!

17:50.880 --> 17:52.960
No one fucking leaves!

17:54.360 --> 17:56.760
[gunshots]

18:02.280 --> 18:03.520
My brother is dead.

18:06.760 --> 18:07.800
You hear me?

18:08.520 --> 18:11.320
My brother is dead!

18:12.240 --> 18:14.800
[panting]

18:27.160 --> 18:28.440
-Tommy.
-[both grunting]

18:56.160 --> 18:58.440
[horse neighing]

20:07.200 --> 20:09.280
[indistinct conversations]

20:17.160 --> 20:18.920
[telephone rings]

20:21.160 --> 20:22.160
Hello, Michael.

20:23.240 --> 20:24.560
There's been a change of plan.

20:25.640 --> 20:26.960
Mr. Gold will come and get you.

20:28.240 --> 20:29.200
Arthur's dead.

20:39.920 --> 20:41.200
[door closes]

20:55.360 --> 20:57.840
[sighs] Tommy, I've been trying
to think of words...

20:57.920 --> 20:58.920
Don't.

21:01.200 --> 21:02.320
Words don't work.

21:04.760 --> 21:07.080
Michael, we're in a grave situation.

21:08.000 --> 21:09.080
Tommy has a plan.

21:10.760 --> 21:12.280
Instead of going to Australia,

21:12.840 --> 21:14.040
you're going to New York.

21:18.320 --> 21:19.160
Why?

21:20.120 --> 21:22.880
'Cause the company has business
to attend to in America.

21:26.680 --> 21:27.760
Will I be coming back?

21:30.840 --> 21:32.240
Train leaves in an hour, Michael.

21:37.520 --> 21:38.640
You made a choice.

21:40.880 --> 21:42.280
You knew I was gonna be shot

21:43.760 --> 21:45.120
and you chose not to tell me.

21:48.160 --> 21:49.320
I chose my mum.

21:52.680 --> 21:54.320
When all this business is over,

21:55.160 --> 21:57.440
we'll all be free to make our own choices.

22:02.240 --> 22:03.160
So is that it?

22:08.200 --> 22:11.400
You get the train to Liverpool,
then the SS Monroe. [clears throat]

22:13.040 --> 22:14.320
Boat sails tomorrow.

22:18.400 --> 22:19.400
Now you can go.

22:54.320 --> 22:55.520
[exhales]

23:13.560 --> 23:15.320
I need an overseas connection, please.

23:16.760 --> 23:17.640
USA.

23:20.520 --> 23:23.040
[breathes deeply]

23:49.840 --> 23:51.960
-[man] Tommy!
-It's all right, let her come.

24:02.200 --> 24:03.120
Please.

24:04.720 --> 24:05.720
Once we're all finished.

24:22.120 --> 24:23.760
[lighter clicks]

24:23.840 --> 24:25.120
[fire burning]

24:25.200 --> 24:28.280
[Audrey] Your note talked about
making terms for peace.

24:29.040 --> 24:31.680
But my son says there are no terms.

24:34.000 --> 24:36.520
You took my husband and my son.

24:37.960 --> 24:39.640
We took two of your brothers.

24:43.320 --> 24:44.480
The vendetta is done.

24:44.760 --> 24:47.400
We say the vendetta is won.

24:48.520 --> 24:50.880
We will take everything you have.

24:51.840 --> 24:53.280
All your businesses,

24:53.640 --> 24:54.960
signed over to us.

24:56.600 --> 24:57.960
You agree to this

24:59.280 --> 25:01.920
or my son will kill you all,

25:03.000 --> 25:04.400
one by one.

25:06.240 --> 25:07.360
The vendetta is won.

25:09.280 --> 25:10.120
That's it.

25:12.760 --> 25:13.680
No more killing.

25:16.520 --> 25:20.520
Who do you think you were, Mr. Shelby?

25:24.800 --> 25:27.080
[banging]

25:28.640 --> 25:30.640
[door unlocks]

25:48.480 --> 25:50.920
Why don't you let him know
we're here to buy his business?

25:51.400 --> 25:52.720
Mr. Solomons!

25:53.560 --> 25:55.560
Mr. Changretta's here to see you!

26:03.440 --> 26:04.280
[speaking Italian]

26:07.360 --> 26:08.320
But why?

26:09.840 --> 26:12.640
Did the Jew fight in France?

26:13.320 --> 26:14.720
[in English]
They say he was a captain.

26:15.280 --> 26:16.280
Oh, yeah?

26:16.880 --> 26:19.920
Then you might wanna tell them
not to open that fucking door.

26:20.000 --> 26:23.560
[speaking Italian]
Hey you, leave that fucking door alone!

26:28.320 --> 26:30.480
Son of a bitch.

26:32.080 --> 26:35.000
[Luca speaking English]
Seems Mr. Solomons already left town.

26:37.080 --> 26:38.600
So all this is mine.

26:39.680 --> 26:41.440
[laughing]

26:45.040 --> 26:45.880
Huh.

27:11.320 --> 27:12.560
[door opens]

27:13.720 --> 27:14.720
[Tommy] You don't knock?

27:15.360 --> 27:16.800
[Lizzie] You don't know my new address?

27:17.000 --> 27:18.320
Hello, Lizzie, how are you?

27:18.440 --> 27:19.760
I know your new address, Lizzie,

27:19.840 --> 27:21.680
because it was me who bought you
the new fucking house.

27:21.760 --> 27:23.160
Then why don't you visit it?

27:33.360 --> 27:34.560
[drawer opens]

27:35.280 --> 27:36.680
[drawer closes]

27:37.680 --> 27:38.760
Yeah, I've been busy.

27:40.480 --> 27:41.560
Busy doing what?

27:46.200 --> 27:47.360
Preparing for tomorrow.

27:48.400 --> 27:49.440
Why, what's tomorrow?

27:50.800 --> 27:54.080
Luca Changretta is coming to Birmingham.
It's our turn.

27:54.160 --> 27:56.800
He's already taken over
Alfie Solomons, Sabini,

27:57.120 --> 27:59.320
Titanics... All of them.

28:01.480 --> 28:04.600
And now he's coming to take control
of Shelby Company Limited.

28:07.640 --> 28:09.160
What are we going to do about that?

28:11.360 --> 28:12.440
We're gonna let him have it.

28:37.680 --> 28:40.560
[footsteps approaching]

29:08.720 --> 29:11.240
[speaking Italian]
Look at them.

29:14.600 --> 29:18.080
All that's left of the Peaky
fucking Blinders.

29:31.240 --> 29:32.120
[snaps]

29:40.000 --> 29:43.960
I've had my lawyer draw up these papers.

29:45.800 --> 29:49.960
Cover every enterprise in your possession.

29:52.080 --> 29:55.440
Bars, restaurants, warehouses.

29:58.000 --> 30:03.360
Every fucking thing that you've taken
all these years to gather together.

30:06.720 --> 30:08.560
You will sign them all over...

30:10.120 --> 30:11.440
to my family

30:15.480 --> 30:16.960
or you're gonna die.

30:18.040 --> 30:19.000
Right here.

30:28.040 --> 30:29.840
I would've buried you all,

30:32.720 --> 30:34.520
but my mother, she, uh...

30:34.720 --> 30:36.800
She knows you. She said,

30:39.280 --> 30:42.040
it'll be worse for you
if I let you live...

30:44.560 --> 30:46.800
and take away everything that you have.

30:54.320 --> 30:55.280
Search them.

31:05.480 --> 31:08.040
Especially don't trust this bitch.

31:33.120 --> 31:33.960
So...

31:37.560 --> 31:38.600
Sign.

31:40.000 --> 31:41.880
Every fucking one of them.

31:48.280 --> 31:50.480
You can sign them on your knees.

31:52.280 --> 31:53.360
On the floor.

31:53.640 --> 31:55.520
[papers falling]

32:04.320 --> 32:08.000
Get on your fucking knees and sign.

32:11.720 --> 32:13.320
A friend of mine once said...

32:14.800 --> 32:16.120
[exhales deeply]

32:16.720 --> 32:18.160
"Big fucks small."

32:19.640 --> 32:21.640
So I had to find someone bigger than you.

32:23.160 --> 32:25.640
Now, you may know
there are two families in Brooklyn,

32:26.240 --> 32:27.760
who want to take over your monopoly

32:27.840 --> 32:29.800
on the import of liquor into New York.

32:30.120 --> 32:32.280
[Polly] But if they move
against you in New York,

32:33.120 --> 32:35.560
they'll start a war between the families.

32:36.960 --> 32:40.080
[Tommy] But if you were to die
in a vendetta

32:40.880 --> 32:43.880
with some fucking bookmaker in Birmingham,

32:44.880 --> 32:47.040
they could take over your business
without a war.

32:49.080 --> 32:52.320
We also contacted
a businessman in Chicago.

32:56.080 --> 33:00.440
He's also interested in moving
into the liquor business in New York.

33:01.560 --> 33:03.360
His name is Alphonse Capone.

33:06.560 --> 33:08.520
You been talking to that fat fuck?

33:09.520 --> 33:11.480
You see, all the blood relatives
you brought with you

33:11.560 --> 33:15.800
from New York, they're all dead,
Mr. Changretta.

33:16.400 --> 33:17.560
And these men here,

33:18.000 --> 33:20.040
they work for money,
for the highest bidder.

33:21.280 --> 33:22.560
They now have new orders.

33:24.960 --> 33:25.880
[Luca] Is that right?

33:31.480 --> 33:32.520
Is that right?

33:36.720 --> 33:38.560
And you, Matteo?

33:54.880 --> 33:55.720
Hey...

33:57.320 --> 33:58.720
Very fucking...

33:59.880 --> 34:01.000
[grunting]

34:09.920 --> 34:12.080
[grunting]

34:23.480 --> 34:24.520
[gasps]

34:34.239 --> 34:37.120
[Tommy] Arthur's been injured,
but he's all right, Poll.

34:39.199 --> 34:42.360
We need to make them believe
that he's dead.

34:44.800 --> 34:48.880
To everyone but you, me, and Linda,

34:49.639 --> 34:51.880
Arthur Shelby is dead.

34:53.880 --> 34:55.239
I've got it all worked out.

34:56.040 --> 34:59.200
We can use his death to win this war.

35:07.320 --> 35:08.640
[thuds]

35:10.600 --> 35:13.200
[exhales deeply]
Tell your people in Chicago

35:14.080 --> 35:18.480
that Michael Gray will sign
the import license to New York.

35:18.920 --> 35:21.600
Three hundred barrels
of English dry gin a month.

35:23.360 --> 35:24.280
Leave.

35:25.120 --> 35:26.000
All of ya.

35:29.200 --> 35:31.320
Tell your boss what you saw here today.

35:32.000 --> 35:32.880
And tell him...

35:36.280 --> 35:38.760
You don't fuck with the Peaky Blinders.

35:43.560 --> 35:46.480
[slow music playing]

35:48.280 --> 35:51.320
[indistinct chatter]

36:01.720 --> 36:03.280
[Tommy] Nice. Hey!

36:04.360 --> 36:05.880
[clears throat] Listen up. Um...

36:06.440 --> 36:09.800
Before we go and eat,
I'd like to say a few words.

36:11.240 --> 36:12.640
Last time we were all here,

36:14.800 --> 36:15.840
it ended badly.

36:16.760 --> 36:17.680
Yeah.

36:18.640 --> 36:20.000
And now, we're in a happier place.

36:23.720 --> 36:27.080
That's it. I'd just like to raise a toast.

36:27.720 --> 36:28.560
[Arthur] Hold on.

36:29.440 --> 36:31.360
A few words I want to say from the heart,

36:31.800 --> 36:33.080
and this time,

36:33.520 --> 36:35.200
you're gonna let me finish, Tommy.

36:37.120 --> 36:38.360
Now, as you all know,

36:39.600 --> 36:42.200
Arthur Shelby is dead.

36:43.200 --> 36:44.240
'Cause of that,

36:45.800 --> 36:47.400
Tommy's offered me a way out.

36:49.000 --> 36:50.160
A new identity.

36:51.480 --> 36:53.480
Start a whole new life for meself.

36:55.200 --> 36:56.360
I've thought about it.

36:59.240 --> 37:00.200
Made a decision.

37:04.880 --> 37:06.800
I ain't fucking going nowhere.

37:06.880 --> 37:08.720
[all laughing]

37:10.240 --> 37:11.680
Our enemies are gone.

37:12.360 --> 37:13.520
Dead, all of them.

37:16.200 --> 37:18.520
For the first time since me,

37:19.920 --> 37:21.200
my two kid brothers,

37:23.080 --> 37:24.720
Tommy and John,

37:26.560 --> 37:28.960
enlisted in the Warwickshire Yeomanry,

37:31.840 --> 37:32.760
we have peace.

37:35.080 --> 37:35.960
So...

37:37.280 --> 37:39.240
I think I'd like to make a proposal

37:41.200 --> 37:43.640
that all of you,
the Shelby Company Limited,

37:44.320 --> 37:47.520
insist that Tommy here

37:48.720 --> 37:50.080
take some time off.

37:51.840 --> 37:53.400
Time you took a holiday, Tom.

37:54.440 --> 37:55.480
Put your feet up.

37:56.960 --> 37:57.960
War's over.

37:58.800 --> 38:00.160
No one wants to kill us.

38:01.360 --> 38:02.240
To peace.

38:03.800 --> 38:05.080
[all] To peace.

38:05.160 --> 38:07.080
[glasses clinking]

38:32.480 --> 38:34.600
I do hope you're gonna leave the dog
out of this.

38:36.040 --> 38:37.360
You were easy to find.

38:38.000 --> 38:39.840
Yeah, well, there's a good reason
for that, Tommy.

38:40.760 --> 38:42.120
Because I wanted it to be here.

38:46.720 --> 38:48.120
I once told you, Alfie,

38:49.480 --> 38:51.880
that for business reasons or in bad blood,

38:52.400 --> 38:53.400
I would kill you.

38:55.640 --> 38:57.440
I have no business reasons.

38:58.560 --> 39:00.440
It seems you have retired.

39:01.840 --> 39:04.560
So, this is all purely for bad blood,
is it, Tommy?

39:04.640 --> 39:06.320
-Yeah.
-Right. Yeah.

39:06.920 --> 39:07.800
Told you.

39:09.000 --> 39:10.400
I wanted it to be here.

39:12.240 --> 39:14.360
-You gonna look after this dog?
-No.

39:14.960 --> 39:16.720
Right then. Well, his name is Cyril

39:17.000 --> 39:18.760
and he'll be very upset and distressed,

39:18.840 --> 39:20.440
so you'll need to find him someone.

39:21.760 --> 39:23.600
-You're not armed?
-No.

39:24.600 --> 39:25.480
Don't be dull.

39:27.000 --> 39:28.960
The only thing I got on me

39:30.000 --> 39:31.640
is fucking cancer, mate.

39:36.400 --> 39:37.280
Yeah.

39:38.720 --> 39:39.760
Riddled with it.

39:40.840 --> 39:44.120
Doctor told me I might have picked it up
in France from the gas or something.

39:45.120 --> 39:46.600
He even showed me a photograph...

39:46.680 --> 39:48.360
Alfie, stop talking.

39:48.640 --> 39:50.880
So I said, "Margate" right, and here I am.

39:50.960 --> 39:52.800
-Come on, Tommy.
-Alfie, look at me.

39:52.880 --> 39:55.320
There's an honorable reason now
to pull that trigger...

39:55.400 --> 39:56.880
Alfie, look at me.

39:56.960 --> 39:59.240
Fucking get on with it.
Stop acting like a little girl.

39:59.320 --> 40:00.240
Alfie!

40:00.600 --> 40:02.080
[gunshots]

41:02.560 --> 41:04.880
[somber music playing]

41:36.400 --> 41:38.240
[music continues]

41:52.520 --> 41:55.120
-[horses approaching]
-[explosion]

41:58.600 --> 42:00.920
-[gunshots]
-[dogs barking]

42:02.400 --> 42:03.720
[men shouting]

42:05.200 --> 42:07.120
[dogs barking]

42:12.760 --> 42:14.160
[sighs]

42:26.760 --> 42:28.000
[grunts]

42:31.400 --> 42:32.440
[Frances, muffled] Mr. Shelby.

42:35.640 --> 42:36.680
Mr. Shelby.

42:40.120 --> 42:41.200
[clear] Mr. Shelby.

42:51.160 --> 42:54.000
Mr. Shelby, you are not yourself.
I should call a doctor.

42:58.480 --> 42:59.760
It's all right, Frances.

43:01.640 --> 43:02.720
I'll call Mrs. Gray.

43:05.040 --> 43:06.320
I know what this is...

43:08.160 --> 43:10.560
It's just myself talking to myself
about myself.

43:12.040 --> 43:13.160
[uncorking bottle]

43:13.240 --> 43:14.200
[pouring drink]

43:15.520 --> 43:16.480
All right. Thank you.

43:22.320 --> 43:23.880
[music continues]

44:06.280 --> 44:08.160
[glass shatters]

44:22.880 --> 44:23.840
Charlie.

45:00.480 --> 45:01.920
[clears throat]

45:05.000 --> 45:06.600
Since I know you won't go yourself,

45:07.640 --> 45:09.480
I've been to a doctor on your behalf.

45:11.320 --> 45:13.320
No, it's all right.
None of the boys know you're sick.

45:13.400 --> 45:14.720
[scoffs]

45:18.440 --> 45:19.480
I'm not sick, Polly.

45:26.280 --> 45:28.640
It starts when you stop, when you rest.

45:30.440 --> 45:31.480
Could be nerves.

45:33.560 --> 45:34.400
The war.

45:38.080 --> 45:40.640
It might be the alcohol.
Blue devils, they call that.

45:40.880 --> 45:41.800
Yeah, well. Yeah.

45:42.240 --> 45:43.560
Yeah, it's the fucking booze.

45:44.840 --> 45:47.600
It's the booze, the booze got out
and the booze got in me bones.

45:52.480 --> 45:53.800
Lizzie wants to see you.

45:54.120 --> 45:54.960
No.

45:55.600 --> 45:56.640
Tom, she's showing.

45:56.920 --> 45:58.400
I don't want to see Lizzie, Poll.

46:05.800 --> 46:07.560
Shit. Maybe it's in us.

46:10.960 --> 46:12.120
It's with Shelbys.

46:14.840 --> 46:16.360
It's in our Gypsy blood.

46:18.600 --> 46:20.720
We live somewhere between life and death,

46:22.720 --> 46:24.120
waiting to move on.

46:27.240 --> 46:28.160
And in the end,

46:29.680 --> 46:30.760
we accept it.

46:33.480 --> 46:35.280
We shake hands with devils

46:36.600 --> 46:38.120
and we walk past them.

47:04.600 --> 47:05.520
[sighs]

47:34.240 --> 47:36.200
Mr. Shelby, you're meant to be resting.

47:39.120 --> 47:40.880
I've learned something, Frances.

47:42.800 --> 47:45.320
There's no rest for me in this world.

47:49.600 --> 47:50.840
Perhaps in the next.

47:59.320 --> 48:02.200
Them there, you pay out.
This one, you have to think.

48:02.280 --> 48:03.760
Use your fucking head, man.

48:03.840 --> 48:05.280
Right, even money.

48:05.360 --> 48:07.800
Whose fucking idea was it
that I go on holiday, eh?

48:07.880 --> 48:11.160
Welcome back, Tommy. How was it?
What'd you get up to?

48:11.240 --> 48:12.640
Went fishing, played golf.

48:12.720 --> 48:14.080
Golf's fucking boring.

48:14.160 --> 48:15.240
Boring and easy.

48:15.440 --> 48:17.840
Yeah, well, what's the plan?

48:22.520 --> 48:24.080
[Tommy] I need you
to give this to Jessie Eden.

48:25.040 --> 48:25.920
By hand.

48:26.040 --> 48:27.760
-Yes, Mr. Shelby.
-By your hand.

48:29.120 --> 48:30.920
This will be the last job
you'll do for me.

48:31.320 --> 48:33.240
You can go to Glasgow
and be with your family.

48:34.040 --> 48:34.880
You're free.

48:47.600 --> 48:49.080
You need to sign all of these.

48:59.920 --> 49:01.480
So you shook hands with the devil?

49:06.200 --> 49:07.040
Yeah.

49:08.840 --> 49:09.960
And I walked past him.

49:16.120 --> 49:16.960
Poll...

49:20.120 --> 49:21.280
I've had an idea.

49:22.920 --> 49:23.880
Oh, fuck.

49:30.960 --> 49:34.240
[Tommy] "Dear Jessie,
now, more certainly than ever,

49:34.600 --> 49:37.560
I believe things must change.
Things must change.

49:38.320 --> 49:39.840
The general strike is holding.

49:40.560 --> 49:41.960
We've not an hour to lose.

49:42.840 --> 49:43.680
Meet me."

49:55.000 --> 49:57.200
-[Tommy] I've made up my mind, Jessie.
-[Jessie] About what?

50:02.760 --> 50:04.440
Your cause is now my cause.

50:05.680 --> 50:06.640
I wanna help.

50:07.720 --> 50:10.480
The strike is holding. I want to meet
the people who can take this further.

50:12.800 --> 50:13.840
Are you serious?

50:14.480 --> 50:15.320
Yeah.

50:16.240 --> 50:17.360
I've done a lot of thinking.

50:19.280 --> 50:20.640
Right. I'll arrange a meeting.

50:21.520 --> 50:23.160
The operator knows my voice.

50:23.440 --> 50:24.680
Give me the name and the number.

50:32.400 --> 50:33.720
His name is Casey Douglas.

50:35.960 --> 50:37.720
It's Sparkhill 453.

50:37.840 --> 50:38.720
Right.

50:44.800 --> 50:45.960
And he's the leader of the cell?

50:49.680 --> 50:51.640
He's in contact with London and Moscow.

50:54.640 --> 50:55.480
Good.

51:00.040 --> 51:01.760
Yeah. Sparkhill 453.

51:52.480 --> 51:53.960
[exhales deeply]

52:04.520 --> 52:06.880
[Bigge] You are quite a creature,
Mr. Shelby.

52:08.640 --> 52:12.320
When I received your note,
I wasn't sure you could deliver.

52:17.720 --> 52:18.840
I've made contact

52:20.200 --> 52:23.320
with a Soviet agent inside
the Birmingham Communist Party.

52:26.200 --> 52:27.400
And do you have a name?

52:28.240 --> 52:31.040
And an address and a telephone number.

52:35.760 --> 52:37.240
I can be of great use to you.

52:39.200 --> 52:41.720
I can give you the name
of any communist party member,

52:42.560 --> 52:45.120
who is prepared to cross the line
into armed revolution.

52:45.920 --> 52:48.240
We're in the fourth day
of a general strike,

52:48.320 --> 52:49.600
which appears to be holding.

52:51.000 --> 52:52.600
Even if it fails today,

52:53.840 --> 52:55.320
tomorrow they may succeed.

52:57.040 --> 52:58.640
Mmm. [sniffs]

53:00.920 --> 53:04.800
And you're offering to help ensure
they never succeed.

53:05.480 --> 53:06.880
If my cover is maintained,

53:08.080 --> 53:11.560
I can begin to shape the movement
and organize it myself.

53:12.400 --> 53:13.880
And undermine it?

53:14.720 --> 53:17.560
Rise through the ranks of the wider
Socialist movements.

53:20.360 --> 53:22.840
Of course you want something in return.

53:24.360 --> 53:27.080
What this time? A knighthood?

53:31.720 --> 53:32.640
My proposal.

53:34.720 --> 53:35.800
And my conditions.

53:39.520 --> 53:42.120
Mmm. For the attention
of Winston Churchill?

53:42.760 --> 53:44.360
He holds me in very high regard.

53:52.440 --> 53:53.680
Are you serious?

53:54.600 --> 53:56.840
Breaking up a revolutionary cell
is one thing.

53:57.920 --> 54:00.400
Given my position of influence
in my home city,

54:01.240 --> 54:03.120
I could be of much more use
to you than that.

54:06.240 --> 54:07.680
[folk music playing]

54:52.280 --> 54:56.480
[returning officer]
Ronald Carr, Conservative, 3,412.

54:56.640 --> 54:59.920
Bernard Hall, Liberal. 4,015.

55:00.520 --> 55:04.760
Michael Ross, Communist. 6,406.

55:05.040 --> 55:10.400
Thomas Shelby, Labour Party. 48,564.

55:10.600 --> 55:13.480
[crowd cheering]

55:14.080 --> 55:15.960
I now declare Thomas Shelby

55:16.080 --> 55:18.240
to be the new Labour Member of Parliament

55:18.320 --> 55:20.800
for the constituency of Birmingham South.

55:22.800 --> 55:24.880
[song continues]

56:07.360 --> 56:09.560
♪ On a gathering storm comes ♪

56:09.640 --> 56:11.400
♪ A tall handsome man ♪

56:11.480 --> 56:13.760
♪ In a dusty black coat with ♪

56:13.840 --> 56:16.160
♪ A red right hand ♪
